  "steps": [
    "To a pan on medium heat, add 2 tbsp mustard oil. Once the oil heats up, add 200g low-fat paneer (whole block). Fry until golden brown on both sides, then set it aside.",
    "In the same oil, add 2 finely chopped onions and sauté until golden brown. In the meantime, chop the fried paneer into cubes.",
    "Once the onions brown, add 1 tsp chilli garlic paste and sauté for 2 minutes. Now add 1 handful fresh coriander, 1 chopped green chilli, ½ tsp turmeric powder, 1 tsp Kashmiri red chilli powder, 1¼ tsp coriander powder, 1 tsp salt, Mix everything really well until the spices are nicely combined.",
    "Now add 3 tbsp yogurt and 100ml water. Give it a good stir. Add the fried paneer cubes back into the pan. Sprinkle in 1 tsp brown sugar and add 2 tbsp fresh cream.",
    "Mix everything well and let it simmer until the gravy thickens and coats the paneer beautifully.",
    "Garnish with ½ handful of fresh coriander, and it’s ready to serve!"
  ],
